"""Compiled checks for AELLO-C8-S2. GENERATED by solution/recompute.py. DO NOT HAND-EDIT.

What is graded here is a PROGRAM and a MEMORY, not an array. train.py is executed once per graded
configuration and timed host-side; carry/notes.json is the only byte-durable channel between one
attempt and the next, and it is 2,048 bytes wide, closed-schema and expiring. These checks
establish that the program is a program rather than a serialized model, that the store is a
calibration table rather than a weight cache or a forged provenance record, that the clock opened
where it was supposed to, and that the configurations graded are the ones the published schedule
selects -- before any speed is credited. Every check runs against delivered bytes and references
no unmeasured quantity, except bar_gated_wallclock_ramp_over_the_scored_attempt, which raises ConstantUnmeasured while
tests/constants.json carries nulls.
"""
